# Tailwind CSS v4 rules

Apply this rule only when the repository uses Tailwind CSS v4 or the `@tailwindcss/postcss` integration. Do not apply it to Tailwind v3 or non-Tailwind CSS.

- Entry CSS is `@import "tailwindcss";` — NOT the v3 `@tailwind base/components/utilities` trio.
- Do not add the v3 `autoprefixer` or `postcss-nested` setup. Tailwind v4’s Lightning CSS pipeline handles the needed transforms.
- Design tokens live in a `@theme { }` block in CSS, not in `tailwind.config.js`.
- Use tokens, not arbitrary values: `bg-brand-500`, not `bg-[#3b82f6]`, unless a one-off value is genuinely required and documented.
- Container queries are built in (`@container`, `@sm:`). Do not install the container-queries plugin.

References:
- Tailwind CSS v4 upgrade guide: https://tailwindcss.com/docs/upgrade-guide
- Tailwind theme variables: https://tailwindcss.com/docs/theme
- Tailwind responsive and container queries: https://tailwindcss.com/docs/responsive-design
